

-> What is Annotation-Based Configuration?
    In annotation-based configuration, we use annotations in Java classes to tell Spring:
        which class is a bean
        how dependencies are injected
        how components are scanned
    So no XML file for bean definitions.

-> Why Annotations Are Preferred Over XML?

    | XML Configuration | Annotation Configuration      |
    | ----------------- | ----------------------------- |
    | Too verbose       | Clean & readable              |
    | Separate file     | Configuration stays with code |
    | Hard to maintain  | Easy to maintain              |
    | Error-prone       | Compile-time safety           |
